A step SQLite refuses (a column misspelt): the migration rolls back, the
database is as it was, recording nothing, and no copy is left. The error
names the step.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup');

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== ledger
UPDATE dish SET title = upper(titel);

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, ledger.sql's step 1
  step 1
    UPDATE dish SET title = upper(titel);

== error
migrating test.db: ledger.sql's step 1: no such column: titel (a step runs on the database as the last deploy left it, before schema.sql's changes)
